  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Question": "A parabola opening to the right has its focus at \\((2,0)\\). What is \\(2p\\)?",
  "Choices": {},
  "Correct Answer": "8",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "The vertex is not specified. If the vertex is assumed to be \\((0,0)\\), the standard equation \\(y^2=2px\\), with \\(p>0\\), has focus \\((p/2,0)\\). Thus \\(p/2=2\\), so \\(p=4\\) and \\(2p=8\\).\n\nFor a different example, translate \\(y^2=4x\\), whose focus is \\((1,0)\\), one unit to the right. This gives \\(y^2=4(x-1)\\), with focus \\((2,0)\\) and \\(2p=4\\). It also opens right. Both parabolas satisfy the stated conditions, so \\(2p\\) is not uniquely determined. The keyed answer \\(8\\) requires the additional assumption that the vertex is the origin.",
